<h1>&nbsp&nbsp VR Products</h1>
<br>
<h5><b>&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp 1. Sony PlayStation VR
BEST FOR PLAYSTATION 4 OWNERS
</h5>
<div class="row">
  <div class="column ">
    &nbsp&nbsp <img src="B7.png" alt="" style="width:110%; margin-top:35px;" >
<div style="position:absolute; left:650px; top:350px;">
	<p style="font-size:28px;">
	<p><h5>The Sony PlayStation VR headset brings powerful, compelling virtual reality, with motion control support, to the PlayStation 4.
US Street Price$399.99
</h5></p>
<dl>
   <ol><dt>PROS:<dt/>
      <ul> <dd><li>Immersive VR experience</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Works with non-VR apps and games</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Motion control support</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Low cost of entry compared with PC-based headsets</li></dd>
	   </ul></ol>
</dl>
<dl>
   <ol><dt>CONS:<dt/>
      <ul> <dd><li>Requires PlayStation Camera, which is not included</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Slightly less powerful than its main competitors</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Some motion-tracking hiccups when playing in brightly lit rooms</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Low cost of entry compared with PC-based headsets</dd>
	   </ul></ol>
</dl>

</div>
	</div> 

<h5><b><br>
<br> 2.Valve index VR kit</h5></b>

  <div class="column ">
    &nbsp&nbsp <img src="B8.jpg" alt="" style="width:110%; margin-top:35px;" >
<div style="position:absolute; left:650px; top:820px;">
	<p style="font-size:28px;"><h5>  BEST FOR IMMERSIVE PC VR GAMING </h5>
	The Valve Index is the most impressive consumer VR headset we've seen yet, entirely due to its revolutionary, finger-tracking controllers.
US Street Price$999.00
</h5></p>

<dl>
   <ol><dt>PROS:<dt/>
      <ul><dd><li>Immersive, finger-tracking controllers</li></dd>
       <dd><li>High, 120Hz refresh rate delivers smooth motion</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Lots of VR software available on PC via SteamVR </li></dd>
        </ul></ol>
</dl>
<dl>
   <ol><dt>CONS:<dt/>
      <ul> <dd><li>Expensive.</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Slightly less powerful than its main competitors</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Occasionally frustrating tethered design</li></dd>
	   </ul></ol>
</dl>
</div>
</div>

<h5><b><br>
<br>3.	HTC Vive Pro 2</h3></b>

  <div class="column ">
    &nbsp&nbsp <img src="B9.png" alt="" style="width:110%; margin-top:35px;" >
<div style="position:absolute; left:650px; top:1250px;">
	<p style="font-size:28px;"><h5><b> BEST FOR HIGH END PC VR</b></h5>
	<br>
The Vive Pro 2 is the highest-resolution VR headset we've seen yet, with a price to match. It's worth considering if you want the
best VR experience available, and don't mind mixing and matching components.US Street Price$799.00
</h5></p>

<dl>
   <ol><dt>PROS:<dt/>
      <ul><dd><li>The best resolution for VR gaming</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Smooth motion tracking</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Works with Valve Index controllers</li></dd>
        </ul></ol>
</dl>
<dl>
   <ol><dt>CONS:<dt/>
      <ul> <dd><li>Expensive</li></dd>
       <dd><li>Doesn't include necessary base stations or controllers</li></dd>
	   </ul></ol>

</div>
</div>
